message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a decorative wire pumpkin with artificial foliage. Such items are typically classified as festive articles under 9505.90, since a Halloween/autumn decoration is a festive article. The 9505.90.6000 subheading covers "Other" festive, carnival or other entertainment articles. The alternative, 9505.10 (Christmas articles), does not apply to a pumpkin. Under the current HTSUS, 9505.90.60 is "Other" with a 00 statistical suffix.

The competing classification is as an artificial flower or foliage under 6702, but the essential character of a pumpkin-shaped wire frame is a festive decoration. Fall harvest decorations have been ruled festive articles under 9505 when they relate to Halloween or Thanksgiving. Pumpkins are associated with Halloween and Thanksgiving, so 9505.90.6000 is the likely answer.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The wire pumpkin with artificial autumn foliage is a composite decorative article whose essential character is a festive (Halloween/harvest season) decoration, so it falls in heading 9505 as other festive articles."}
